---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { NOTICE, effectiveLabel, groupLabel, privacyEmail } from "../lib/notice";

const email = privacyEmail();
const effective = effectiveLabel();
const group = groupLabel();
// One string, so formatting cannot add spaces inside the brackets.
const oaic = `(<a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>)`;
---

<Base
  title="GOD Group Privacy Notice | GOD (Global Omni Data)"
  description="How the GOD group combines what you do in YourTal, SnapApp and Free Tax Returns into one profile, what businesses receive, and your choices. Includes a short version for teens."
  ogImage="/og/privacy.png"
>
  <PageHero
    kicker={`Version ${NOTICE.version}, effective ${effective}`}
    title="GOD Group Privacy Notice"
    lede="How the GOD group combines what you do in our apps, and what that means for you."
    crumbs={[
      { href: "/", label: "Home" },
      { href: "/privacy/", label: "Trust and privacy" },
      { label: "Group Privacy Notice" },
    ]}
  >
    <a class="btn btn-line" href="#teens">
      For teens
    </a>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="sec" id="adult">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="notice">
        <section id="who-we-are">
          <h2>Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            YourTal, SnapApp and Free Tax Returns are brands of {group}. In this notice "we" means
            the GOD group.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="what-this-covers">
          <h2>What this notice covers</h2>
          <p>
            It explains how the GOD group combines what you do in our apps into one profile, and how
            we use that profile to give businesses insight about their markets. Each app's own
            privacy policy still explains how that app runs your account.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="what-we-combine">
          <h2>What we combine</h2>
          <p>
            If you use more than one of our apps, we connect your accounts into one profile. We
            combine:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              from YourTal: your age group, the area you chose, the interests you chose, the
              campaigns you watch and save, and the points and vouchers you earn and use;
            </li>
            <li>
              from SnapApp: what you buy and where, read from the receipts you scan (the shop, its
              address, the date, the amount and the type of purchase);
            </li>
            <li>
              from Free Tax Returns: your postcode, occupation, income range and the status of your
              return.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We never combine your name, email address, phone number, passwords, tax file number,
            bank details, identity documents, receipt images or the detail of your tax return into
            this profile.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="location">
          <h2>Where the location comes from</h2>
          <p>
            We know where a shop is from the address on your receipt. We do not track your phone's
            location for this.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="what-we-work-out">
          <h2>What we work out</h2>
          <p>
            From your combined profile we work out your likely home and activity areas, your
            interests, your spending pattern by category, and which shops and brands you return to.
            We use this to describe groups of people. We do not use it to make decisions about you
            that have legal or similarly significant effects.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="what-businesses-receive">
          <h2>What businesses receive</h2>
          <p>
            Businesses receive reports about groups of people, for example "38% of this café's
            customers live within these six suburbs and 61% are aged 25 to 44". A business never
            receives your profile, your name or any detail that identifies you. Groups smaller than
            10 people are never shown to a business. We do not sell lists of people.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="sensitive-purchases">
          <h2>Health and other sensitive purchases</h2>
          <p>
            Purchases that may reveal your health, religion, sexuality or financial difficulty are
            never used to build a profile of you. They are only counted in large groups.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="who-can-see">
          <h2>Who can see your profile</h2>
          <p>
            A small number of GOD staff, each of whom has signed a written confidentiality
            agreement, can open a profile to check that our processing is correct. Profiles carry a
            code instead of your name. Every time a profile is opened, the reason is recorded.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="where-kept">
          <h2>Where your data is kept</h2>
          <p>
            On servers in Indonesia, run by our hosting provider, Hostinger. This means your data
            is sent outside Australia to be stored. We protect it with access controls, encryption
            in transit, passkey sign-in for staff, and audit logs. If we move it to another
            country, we will update this notice and ask you to accept it again.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="how-long">
          <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>
            Detailed activity is kept for 24 months. Group totals, which do not identify anyone, may
            be kept longer. If you delete your account in any of our apps, your data is removed from
            the combined profile within {NOTICE.deletionWindow}.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="your-choices">
          <h2>Your choices</h2>
          <p>
            You can ask to see the data we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or delete your
            account in any app. To stop your data being combined without deleting your account, ask
            us through the app's account deletion or request form, or
            <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>contact us</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="complaints">
          <h2>Complaints</h2>
          <p>
            Contact our privacy officer at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We reply within
            30 days. If you are not satisfied, you can complain to the Office of the Australian
            Information Commissioner <Fragment set:html={oaic} />.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes">
          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            If we change this notice in a way that affects you, we will ask you to accept the new
            version the next time you sign in.
          </p>
          <p>
            Version 1.1 (27 November 2026) corrects where your data is kept: Indonesia, not
            Australia as version 1.0 said. Nothing else changed.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec tint" id="teens">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="notice">
        <h2>For teens: how GOD uses your activity</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>YourTal, SnapApp and Free Tax Returns belong to one group called GOD.</li>
          <li>
            If you use more than one of them, we put your activity together: the area you chose, the
            things you like and watch, and what you buy and where (from your receipts).
          </li>
          <li>
            We use it to tell businesses about groups of young people, like "teens near Parramatta
            often buy at these kinds of shops". We only do this for groups of at least 20.
          </li>
          <li>
            No business ever sees you, your name or your own activity. Nobody uses this to pick ads
            for you.
          </li>
          <li>We never use anything about alcohol, vapes, gambling or health for teens.</li>
          <li>
            Your parent or guardian agreed to this when they set up your account. Either of you can
            ask us about it or delete your account at any time.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .notice {
    max-width: 44rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
  }
  .notice h2 {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .notice p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .notice p + p,
  .notice p + ul,
  .notice ul + p {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .notice ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .notice a {
    color: var(--indigo-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .notice section[id],
  #teens {
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  #teens .notice {
    gap: 20px;
  }
</style>
